# Security response headers for the Cloudflare Pages deployment.
# Cloudflare serves this file verbatim (it is copied from public/ into dist/ at build).
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# CSP notes (validated against the production build, 2026-06-30; revised 2026-07-28):
#   - script-src 'self' + one sha256 + static.cloudflareinsights.com — see the Web Analytics
#                              note below. The Vite build itself emits only external module
#                              chunks from our origin and no inline <script>.
#   - style-src 'unsafe-inline' — the theming layer is an inline-style-object model, and the
#                              Google Fonts stylesheet is loaded from fonts.googleapis.com.
#   - connect-src ...supabase.co — Supabase REST (https) + Realtime (wss).
#   - connect-src fonts.*      — the SERVICE WORKER's own fetch() for the Google Fonts stylesheet
#                              and font files. See the scoped-block post-mortem below.
#   - img-src data:            — Vite may inline small SVG assets as data: URIs.
# If the Cloudflare preview deploy shows CSP violations in the console, relax the offending
# directive (or switch to Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only to observe first).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY connect-src TRUSTS THE FONT HOSTS SITE-WIDE (post-mortem, 2026-07-28)
#
# The page's own <link> to the Google Fonts stylesheet is governed by style-src, which has always
# allowed it. The SERVICE WORKER's fetch() of that same URL is governed by connect-src, which did
# not. Until v1.2.37 this file tried to widen connect-src for the worker alone, via a second rule
# scoped to the /sw.js response path, on the theory that only that one script needed it.
#
# THAT DID NOT WORK, and it is now confirmed in production, not theorised: with the worker active,
# the console showed
#     Failed to load 'https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=...'.
#     A ServiceWorker passed a promise to FetchEvent.respondWith() that rejected with
#     'TypeError: NetworkError when attempting to fetch resource.'
# The scoped block does not replace the site-wide one for a /sw.js request, so the worker's
# fetch stayed bound by the narrower connect-src and was refused.
#
# It only bit RETURNING visitors: on a first visit the worker is not yet controlling the page, the
# fonts load normally and land in the HTTP cache, so a preview-deploy smoke test looks fine. On the
# next visit the worker intercepts, its fetch is blocked, and — because cacheFirst had no
# network-failure fallback — the rejection propagated and the whole stylesheet failed. Typography
# silently fell back to system fonts.
#
# Fix: trust the two font hosts in the site-wide connect-src (they were already trusted for
# style-src/font-src, so nothing new enters the trust set) and delete the scoped block. Do NOT
# reintroduce a per-path CSP rule here expecting it to override this one — it does not.
# src/sw.ts's cacheFirst also gained a fallback so a refused fetch degrades one asset instead of
# failing the page.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLOUDFLARE WEB ANALYTICS
#
# Pages auto-injects the Web Analytics beacon: an inline loader plus a script from
# static.cloudflareinsights.com, which reports to cloudflareinsights.com. Under script-src 'self'
# both were blocked, so analytics collected nothing from the day it was switched on.
#
# The sha256 below is the hash of Cloudflare's injected INLINE loader. It is Cloudflare's snippet,
# not ours, so a beacon update can change it and silently re-break analytics (the page itself keeps
# working — only the beacon fails). If the console reports a blocked inline script again, copy the
# hash the browser prints in that message into script-src here. Nothing else depends on it.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-jgs8w4t+uLh9rWeOIxx1EwRzhZxBbFdg11vxhWHiA8s=' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://fonts.googleapis.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
